_e9155a0f",18,-6,1,"This seems like a hack. Is there a way to fix this on the password manager side instead?"],["ba630f72_5af74e6c",16,-5,1,"If this always returns `false` for PWM, why should password manager even call this method?"]],0,871],[7146169,20404,5,0.385,0.279,[[8,147]],[],0,872],[7146241,20405,2,0.197,0.133,[[8,148]],[],0,873],[7157333,20409,4,0.35,0.251,[[4,457]],[],0,874],[7157587,20409,1,0.217,0.149,[[4,458]],[],0,875],[7156814,20409,2,0.217,0.149,[[4,459]],[],0,876],[7156817,20409,2,0.217,0.149,[[4,460]],[],0,877],[7151046,20409,3,0.197,0.133,[[8,149]],[],0,878],[7157344,20409,3,0.217,0.149,[[4,461]],[],0,879],[7172168,20419,143,5.576,4.507,[[8,0.986,150,142],[17,0.014,5,1]],[["2359b021_a2b47808",55,-7,1,"There is [strong guidance](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:docs/chrome_browser_design_principles.md;l=346-360;drc=f66690411efbdc9f577da23a48ae988dbe1dd4ea) not to use this…"],["2a62006d_a8ef5b11",55,-7,1,"You are not actually checking any mock expectations - can you just override this as empty methods and call the class a `TestWalletablePassBubbleViewBase`?"],["5a3bec3f_c95f2cb8",55,-7,1,"Please always initialize raw pointers to `nullptr` - they are not auto-initialized."],["6371098e_5c173dd0",5,-7,1,"Nit: Please add a bug."],["7f58b020_6077439e",55,-7,1,"Here and everywhere else: Do you have plans for the pass? If not, can you just pass `{}` as an argument to `SetUpAndShowSaveBubble`?"],["920231d4_a6764bb0",55,-7,0,"Nit: Please add `using ::testing::NiceMock` and drop the prefix here.."],["9656ee8d_165a2d82",55,-7,1,"Optional nit here and below: Use `base::test::TestFuture` to make this easier to write and robust against asynchronicity. That is, do something like the following: ```…"],["b65d2958_c93b02c9",55,-7,0,"Doesn't this need an `override`, too?"],["c2d166f0_e3d37196",55,-7,1,"Not needed: Empty. Optional: Just move all of this into the constructor."],["13d6ec16_27987053",55,-1,1,"Optional nit: Make all those members private and expose the only ones that you need in the test (AFAIK just the controller?) via a protected getter. It makes refactoring tests simpler."],["1fdab251_b1b30b9b",55,-1,1,"Optional nit: Adding `using WalletablePassBubbleResult = WalletablePassClient::WalletablePassBubbleResult;` and similarly for the `ClosedReason` would make these statements shorter."],["6d2f7211_d82b565d",56,-1,1,"Why is this CrOS only? I would expect the dependency to go where Autofill's UI unit tests are, i.e. [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/test/BUILD.gn;l=7028;drc=d9bd…"]],0,880],[7150906,20419,89,3.042,2.433,[[8,151]],[["50e4fd8c_e1cbdcf2",57,-10,1,"Does this mean the bubble is not really closed, but just hide temporarily, and will reshow again if the tab is still active?"],["6b6cfd2a_35885e43",57,-10,1,"I have a concern here: - IIUC, the `BubbleManager` will eventually remove the pending bubble if it does not get shown soon enough. - If so, doesn't this mean that a bubble controller cannot guarantee…"],["123dd7ca_90ba6452",55,-6,1,"Not necessary if you add a `SetXForTesting` method to `TabFeatures` for your `BubbleManager`."],["1f31975a_3cb9b7e0",55,-6,1,"Why is that cast needed? Isn't `ShowBubble` part of the interface?"],["4689fc32_a05d16d7",55,-6,1,"Nit: No reason to have the feature list be part of the fixture - just initialized it here ``` base::test::ScopedFeatureList feature_list{yourFeature}; ```"],["4d8e658b_4c195c10",58,-6,1,"Nit: If I look at `tab_features.h`, then this would be the only `virtual` method. All other tests seem to add a `SetXForTesting` method instead. Could you follow the existing pattern just to keep it…"],["958847d4_9211a048",55,-6,1,"Optional nit: Similar feedback to the prior CL - this might read nicer with a `TestFuture`."],["9f3a5753_b48d62da",55,-6,0,"For my understand: Is there an obstruction to using the real `BubbleManager` here? Or would that complicate things much?"],["ebe5db73_0ee5d65f",55,-6,1,"Nit: Use setter instead - see comment above."],["7fd45b24_ed430ebe",55,-1,1,"Nit: Please drop."],["f26c8830_874ed4fa",55,-1,1,"Nit: ```suggestion MockBubbleManager& bubble_manager = *tab_features_.SetBubbleManagerForTesting(std::make_unique<NiceMock<MockBubbleManager>>()); ```"]],0,881],[7157198,20419,36,1.77,1.388,[[8,0.829,152,31],[18,0.171,0,5]],[["7bdfec88_f895c6a8",57,-9,0,"Will it cause the OnBubbleClosed() being executed? Otherwise, we may need to call ResetBubbleViewAndInformBubbleManager() here?"],["1a751f7f_fc45e60d",55,-6,1,"Nit: Not needed."],["7a97d540_2c6bc032",55,-6,1,"Nit: Same comment as in the rest of the chain: If you use a `TestFuture`, then you can just do `future.Get()` and compare the result."],["9655a0a3_34a414a7",55,-6,1,"Nit: Just pass `{}`?"],["e023daa6_ef1e81e0",55,-6,1,"Same nits as in the previous CLs."]],0,882],[7204928,20419,7,0.385,0.279,[[19,0]],[],0,883],[7204929,20419,4,0.385,0.279,[[19,1]],[["322117da_ece1c8ce",59,0,1,"Could you add comment with link to the bug? Same above"]],0,884],[7207280,20419,3,0.169,0.112,[[20,14]],[["faa0f04f_c56774c6",60,0,0,"Could you assign this bug to the test owner?"]],0,885],[7203944,20419,1,0.169,0.112,[[20,15]],[],0,886],[7204396,20423,3,0.197,0.133,[[8,0.429,153,2],[4,0.286,462,1],[10,0.143,35,0],[9,0.143,17,0]],[],0,887],[7213579,20423,1,0.197,0.133,[[8,154]],[["7d448daa_48485b29",41,0,1,"I don't know this code well enough to understand why this is correct. I also don't understand how this change fits to the CL description. Could you explain this a bit more? 😊"]],0,888],[7232475,20430,37,1.506,1.156,[[4,463]],[],0,889]]}